 "definition": "A project scheduling technique that finds the longest chain of dependent tasks, which sets the shortest possible project duration.",
 "description": {
  "text": "An algorithm for scheduling a set of project activities. The critical path is the longest stretch of dependent activities, and its length gives the time needed to finish. It is commonly used with PERT.",
